course: dictionary
lesson: 9062
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word slider can mean a control on a screen, a small burger, a turtle, or a kind of shoe. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Move the slider to make the screen brighter» tells you the slider is a control you move along a line.
explain: Look at the words around it. «A slider in the park pond lies on a log in the sun.» Turtles lie on logs, so here a slider is an animal, not a machine. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try it in place of the word and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Dictionaries list every meaning, numbered, so you can find the one you need. If the context does not settle it, check the entry. A good dictionary will show you the sense the writer probably meant.
fact: A slider is a noun, and it can mean more than one thing.
fact: On a screen or machine, a slider is a control you move along a line to change something, such as the volume or brightness.
fact: A red-eared slider is a kind of turtle, and it is a common pet. Pet sliders must never be let go in park ponds, because they can crowd out the local pond animals.
fact: In the US, sliders can be small burgers or sandwiches, often served at parties.
fact: In the UK, sliders are informal sandals or shoes with no back, often worn at the beach or pool.
exercise: «Move the slider to make the screen brighter.» What is a slider here? | *A control you move along a line to change brightness | A pet turtle | A small burger
exercise: «A slider in the park pond lies on a log in the sun.» What kind of slider is this? | A flip-flop for the beach | A baseball pitch that curves sideways | *A turtle
exercise: At a US party, a friend says, «Have some sliders!» What are sliders here? | A pair of shoes for the beach | A control on a screen | *Small burgers or sandwiches
test: «Turtles cannot make their own body heat, which is why a slider in the park pond lies on a log in the sun.» Why does the slider lie in the sun? | *It needs the sun to warm its body | It is hunting for food under the water | It wants to swim away from the log
test: «Pet red-eared sliders let go in park ponds can crowd out the local pond animals.» What does this sentence teach us? | Sliders are always found in the wild, never as pets | Pet turtles make the best friends for pond animals | *Pet turtles must never be released into park ponds
exam: In «Pull the slider to close the zip, and keep your fingers away from the teeth», which meaning fits best? | A small burger | A baseball pitch that curves | *A thing that slides, the part that pushes the zip teeth together | A control you move along a line to change brightness
